   "data": {
    "hypothesis": "Aging is driven by hyperfunctional mTOR signaling that continues developmental growth, leading to age-related diseases; hallmarks of aging should be arranged hierarchically from molecular to organismal levels.",
    "disproofExplanation": "If aging were caused by molecular damage accumulation, then interventions that reduce damage would extend lifespan, but only interventions that inhibit hyperfunctional signaling (e.g., rapamycin) do so."
   },
